Protein Name: Insulin receptor
Organism: Homo sapiens (Human)
UniProt Accession ID: P06213
Protein Function: The insulin receptor is a receptor tyrosine kinase that binds insulin and activates signaling pathways involved in glucose uptake, metabolism, growth, and cell survival.
Cellular Location: Cell membrane (plasma membrane); extracellular domain faces outside the cell and intracellular domain performs signaling functions.
